RESULT: W3 PASS — the BT HCI path runs over the WHD bus: chip up (WHD), BT
patchram (cybt over WHD backplane), HCI command/event round-trips (TX + BT poll
thread RX), public BD_ADDR = WiFi MAC + 1 stable across 10 cold boots, advertising.

KNOWN / DEFERRED to W4-W6:
- During `bt init`, the app's concurrent WiFi auto-connect (whd_wifi_join) failed
  once — a coexistence/bus-contention signal under simultaneous WiFi+BT bus use.
  The W3 BT bus lock is BT-LOCAL (serializes cybt's own RMW sequences) and does
  NOT yet serialize against WHD's WLAN thread. Cross-WHD bus arbitration + the
  §2.7 corruption envelope are W4/W6.
- BT RX is a 4 ms poll (no host-wake IRQ hook in WHD mode yet); revisit latency
  vs bus-contention in W4.
